inally lifting the packed bag by its handles.\nretention_analysis:\n- <Subject 1> — fully_preserved: retain the exact bag shape, cream canvas texture, leather handles, black snap, text layout, and the three cartoon bear graphics in every shot.\n- <Subject 2> — fully_preserved: retain the identical wooden table texture, warm lighting, and the consistent background perspective.\n- <Picture 1> — fully_preserved: retain its four-stage shot order, camera angles, physical continuity of items, and realistic photography style.\ndetailed_description:\nPhotorealistic live-action product cinematography with crisp fabric texture, realistic leather shine, natural hand movements, and warm indoor lighting. The actions must follow strict linear physical logic. Do NOT teleport objects into the bag. Objects must be inserted sequentially by the hand. Do NOT make the bag float magically; it must be lifted by physically grasping the handles.\n[Shot 1] At 00:00.000, <Picture 1> establishes <Subject 1> on <Subject 2>. In a close-up shot, the camera slowly pushes in. At 00:00.500, a female hand holds a modern silver lunch box and carefully places it into the open bag. This action is quick.\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.500, cut to a slightly higher angle. The lunch box is now fully resting at the bottom inside the bag. The hand pulls away. The camera shows the wide open space and the lunch box resting perfectly. This shot is brief.\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.000, cut to a slightly elevated close-up. The same hand sequentially grabs a clear water bottle and places it into the bag on one side. Then, the hand reaches for a small notebook and slides it into the bag next to the water bottle. After both items are in, the hand moves to the bag opening, grasps the top edges with two hands, pulls the canvas edges together, and firmly fastens the black snap button. This is the longest shot, showing the sequential filling and closing process.\n[Shot 4] At 00:11.500, cut to a medium shot. The bag is closed. Two hands reach out, grasp the brown leather handles, bring the handles together, and then a single hand (or one hand holding both handles) exerts downward force and smoothly lifts the bag off the table, turning it slightly to showcase the front cartoon print and the bag's elegant fullness. The movement must follow gravity and physical resistance.\nMaintain one consistent bag, exact text, correct hand movements, stable camera positions, realistic lighting, and natural physical interactions. No storyboard grid, panel borders, numbers, split screen, duplicated bags, warped handles, mutated text, extra hands, teleporting objects, magical floating, subtitles, or watermarks.\noverall_soundscape:\nQuiet room tone, gentle sounds of the lunch box tapping against canvas, the soft rustling of the bag, the distinct click of the snap button, and the subtle thud when the bag is lifted off the table. No dialogue.\nnon_diegetic_music:\nLight, upbeat, and friendly lo-fi acoustic music at approximately 90 BPM, with a clean, subtle beat that builds slightly as the bag is filled, and resolves warmly as the bag is lifted in the final shot.}"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "提示词", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [396.1351623535156, 264.849853515625], "pos": [210.1815185546875, 5742.45458984375], "id": 2, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.33.2", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 13}, {"outputs": [{"name": "FLOAT", "links": [26], "label": "FLOAT", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "FLOAT"}], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": [15], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveF